  "path": "[REDACTED].java",
  "line": 75,
  "body": "In `load()`, `arrivalDeadlineDate` is assigned the result of `formatter.parse(datePortion, position)` before validating full-token consumption. `SimpleDateFormat.parse(String, ParsePosition)` can return a non-null `Date` even when it stops early (trailing characters), so on failure this method can throw while still leaving a partially-parsed `arrivalDeadlineDate` in the bean. Parse into a local variable and only assign after validation (or explicitly reset to null on failure) so the bean state stays consistent when load fails."
}

